#   tracking of the ISS. EM radiation propagates via inverse-square law.
# Tau choice: TTL 10 / 10 = 1.0 s. The ISS position is updated every few
#   seconds; a 1 s temporal extent reflects the freshness of a 10 s TTL
#   measurement.
# Absorption: 0.0 — EM propagation through near-vacuum LEO has negligible
#   absorption at these ranges.
# Advection: 0.0 — the ISS position measurement has no advective component.
# Force Gate: PASSES. Radar ranging IS an electromagnetic measurement.
#   An organism could evolve echolocation-like sensing at these wavelengths.
# PARSER CONCERN: The wheretheiss.at API returns a SINGLE flat object
#   {"latitude":..., "longitude":..., "altitude":...}, NOT an array.
#   The `map` extractor iterates arrays (JsonVal::Arr); a single object
#   will yield zero samples (parser-def). The ISS position is now covered
#   by JPL Horizons ephemeris (phi/sources.φ line 160: at iss, format
#   ephemeris_binary). Recommended disposition: DECLINE (superseded by
#   ephemeris).
# ALTITUDE SCALE CONCERN: Old `pos ... 1000.0` scaled km→m. The new `map`
#   extractor has no alt_scale directive (only alt_sign, default 1.0).
#   If retained, altitude would be in km, not m.

